Current Data Storage — What You Get
Looking at the actual data produced (output/pages/*.json and master_dataset.csv):

Each page gets:

A JSON file with the full item (≈1085 lines per page for BBC) — includes raw HTML, all extracted fields
A CSV file with flattened representation
One row in master_dataset.csv with 21 curated fields
The problem: The JSON stores EVERYTHING including raw HTML (1MB+ per page). The CSV is readable but has no schema enforcement. There is no relational database, no clean Markdown, no Parquet export, no unified schema enforcement.

Industry Standard Gap Analysis
Capability	Current Status	Industry Standard	Phase 4A Fix
Data Storage	Siloed JSON/CSV files	Relational + Columnar (SQLite + Parquet)	MetadataStore (SQLite) + ParquetExportPipeline
Content Format	Raw HTML + clean_text	Markdown (LLM-ready, 60-80% token reduction)	MarkdownExtractionPipeline
Schema Enforcement	None — fields can be None	Enforced schemas with defaults	UnifiedSchemaEnricher
Asset Metadata	Basic image_assets from parser.py	Structured image + video metadata	MultimodalAssetExtractor
Crawl Tracking	In-memory dict in api.py	Persistent DB (crawl_jobs table)	MetadataStore.crawl_jobs table
Query Capability	Manual file search	SQL queries by domain/crawl_id/type	MetadataStore.query_by_*
ML Pipeline Ready	CSV only (text-heavy)	Columnar Parquet (compressed 70%+)	ParquetExportPipeline
Field Completeness	Empty/unset fields common	All fields present with defaults	UnifiedSchemaEnricher
